{"instrument_id":"mn:ct-morris-2026","state_code":"CT","jurisdiction_name":"Morris","jurisdiction_type":"Town","scope":"multi_sector_data_centers","status":"active","severity_score":4,"technologies":["battery_storage"],"restriction_types":["moratorium"],"evidence_level":"compiled_record","verification":"unverified","source_family":"Moratorium Nation","date_enacted_iso":"2026-05","date_text":null,"current_end_date":null,"description":"Need to evaluate land use, environmental, infrastructure, fire safety, emergency response, groundwater, traffic, noise, visual, electrical infrastructure, and water-use impacts. Adopted. The Commission's own document repository shows the moratorium text moved from a 'generals' (draft/agenda-attachment) filing on 2026-04-15 to a 'regulations' filing dated 2026-05-20, and secondary press reports the Commission approved the moratorium following a public hearing in mid-May 2026. The operative text (Section 6) fixes a 12-month term running from the effective date of adoption, notwithstanding press descriptions of it as a 'two-year moratorium' (which do not match the adopted text I read). Legal basis: Town of Morris Planning and Zoning Commission, Zoning Moratorium on Battery Energy Storage Systems and Data Centers.","severity_basis":null,"counties":["09160"],"evidence":[{"role":"compiled_source","url":"https://github.com/mjbommar/moratorium-data-2026/blob/main/data/moratorium_inventory.csv","access":null}]},
{"instrument_id":"mn:ny-glenville-2025","state_code":"NY","jurisdiction_name":"Glenville","jurisdiction_type":"Town","scope":"renewables_only","status":"extended","severity_score":4,"technologies":["battery_storage"],"restriction_types":["moratorium"],"evidence_level":"compiled_record","verification":"unverified","source_family":"Moratorium Nation","date_enacted_iso":"2025-06-18","date_text":null,"current_end_date":"2026-07-31","description":"Extended, but that extension has itself now lapsed with no confirmed further action. As of a March 9, 2026 Planning & Zoning Commission meeting, town staff said the Town Board's BESS moratorium 'runs through the end of July 2026' -- a real extension past the original 2025-10-16 end date -- while a draft BESS local law (based on NYSERDA guidance and the Rotterdam model law) was still being refined by the Environmental Conservation Commission and had not been forwarded to PZC for formal review. No news or primary source confirming a further extension, adoption of the permanent law, or expiration past July 2026 was found as of 2026-09-23. Legal basis: Town of Glenville local law (BESS moratorium).","severity_basis":null,"counties":["09190"],"evidence":[{"role":"compiled_source","url":"https://github.com/mjbommar/moratorium-data-2026/blob/main/data/moratorium_inventory.csv","access":null}]},
